Project Planning & Management
1. Testing Scope
In Scope
Functional Testing
Testing the core functionalities of the Hospital and Blood Bank System to ensure that all features work according to the specified requirements.
•	User registration and login
•	Password reset and account management
•	Donor registration and donor profile management
•	Hospital and institution registration and profile management
•	Donation request creation and management
•	Donation response creation and management
•	Blood donation recording and management
•	Blood bag registration and tracking
•	Blood bag status management
•	Blood type and blood component management
•	Blood request creation and management
•	Blood availability checking
•	Blood request approval and status tracking
•	Matching blood requests with available blood bags
•	Donation voucher creation and management
•	Supporting document upload and validation
•	Caregiver assignment and management
•	QR code scanning and blood bag verification
•	Payment processing where applicable
•	Notifications and status updates
•	User profile management
•	Role-based access and permissions
•	Hospital and blood bank data management
UI/UX Testing
Testing the user interface and user experience of the Hospital and Blood Bank System to ensure that it is clear, consistent, accessible, and easy to use.
•	Layout consistency across the system
•	Clear navigation between hospital and blood bank functions
•	Responsive design
•	Proper alignment of fields, tables, buttons, and forms
•	Consistency of colors, fonts, labels, and icons
•	Clear display of blood types and blood bag information
•	User-friendly donation and blood request forms
•	Clear status indicators for donations, blood requests, and blood bags
•	Proper error and validation messages
•	Accessibility and readability of important medical information
•	Consistent interface across different system modules
Security Testing
Testing the system to ensure that sensitive healthcare, donor, hospital, and blood bank information is properly protected.
•	Secure authentication and login
•	Authorization and role-based access control
•	Protection of donor and patient information
•	Protection of hospital and blood bank information
•	Password security
•	Data encryption
•	SQL Injection testing
•	Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) testing
•	Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) testing
•	Session management and timeout
•	Prevention of unauthorized access to medical and blood bank data
•	Validation of user permissions for different roles
Performance Testing
Testing the system performance under normal and high workloads.
•	Page and screen loading time
•	API response time
•	Blood availability search response time
•	Blood request processing performance
•	Blood bag search and tracking performance
•	Database query performance
•	Load testing with multiple users
•	Stress testing under high numbers of requests
•	Performance of QR code scanning and verification
•	System stability during concurrent hospital and blood bank operations
Mobile Compatibility Testing
Testing the system on mobile devices to ensure that hospital staff, donors, and other users can access the system effectively.
•	Android compatibility
•	iOS compatibility
•	Different mobile screen sizes
•	Responsive layouts
•	Touch interactions
•	Buttons and forms on mobile screens
•	QR code scanning functionality
•	Mobile navigation
•	Blood request and donation functionality on mobile devices
•	Proper display of blood bag and donation information
Out of Scope
The following areas are outside the scope of testing:
•	Functionality of third-party systems
•	Testing of non-production environments beyond the required test environment
•	Physical hardware and hospital infrastructure testing
•	Medical equipment functionality
•	Blood storage equipment and refrigeration systems
•	Internet service provider infrastructure
•	SEO and digital marketing
•	Content quality unrelated to system functionality
•	Physical blood testing and laboratory procedures
•	Medical diagnosis or clinical decision-making
•	Physical blood collection procedures
