3. Risk Identification
Personal / Human Risks
•	Lack of experience or training in healthcare and blood bank systems
•	Human errors during test execution
•	Incorrect test data entry
•	Unavailability of team members
•	Poor communication between team members
•	Misunderstanding of hospital and blood bank requirements
•	Incorrect interpretation of blood-related business rules
•	Lack of knowledge of specific user roles and permissions
Environmental Risks
•	Power outages or hardware failures
•	Natural disasters
•	Unstable internet connection
•	Inaccessible testing environment
•	Server downtime
•	Database connection failures
•	Problems with mobile devices used for testing
•	QR scanning problems caused by device cameras
•	Limited access to test environments or required services
Project Risks
•	Unclear or changing requirements
•	Scope creep
•	Tight deadlines
•	Insufficient testing resources
•	Limited test data
•	Budget limitations
•	Delays in development
•	Lack of stakeholder engagement
•	Changes in hospital or blood bank workflows
•	Integration issues between system modules
•	Defects discovered late in the development lifecycle
